    "helpHtml": "<h3>🎯 Battlefield Goal</h3>\n        <p>The central <strong>reactor core</strong> is the station's lifeline. Enemy ships spawn on the outer ring and spiral inward. Your job is not to spam towers — it is to turn limited scrap into a three-ring intercept net that holds for 20 waves (including BOSS).</p>\n        <h3>⚔️ Match Rhythm</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Deploy:</strong> Decide how outer long-range, mid control, and inner cleanup share roles</li>\n          <li><strong>Combat:</strong> Kills become scrap; upgrades and patching matter more than blind next-wave</li>\n          <li><strong>Cleanup:</strong> Do not panic-upgrade leftovers; read which ring is actually failing</li>\n          <li><strong>Wave control:</strong> Auto-next is convenient, but manual pacing usually grows economy better</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🛰️ Ring Logic</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Outer:</strong> Long range — Rail / Nova for early chip damage</li>\n          <li><strong>Mid:</strong> Control core — Frost and AoE create time windows</li>\n          <li><strong>Inner:</strong> Last line — slower is fine if the core never eats hits</li>\n          <li><strong>Upgrade:</strong> In upgrade mode, dump scrap into the tower that is actually clogging a lane</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏭 Build Logic</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Pulse:</strong> Opener clear and positioning tool</li>\n          <li><strong>Salvage:</strong> Economy engine — weak DPS, but missing it starves late game</li>\n          <li><strong>Frost:</strong> Slows the spiral so other towers get more shots</li>\n          <li><strong>Rail:</strong> Burst answer for tanky targets and flagships</li>\n          <li><strong>Nova:</strong> Dense formations and mid/late mixed fleets</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>👾 Threat Read</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Shard / Ghost:</strong> Tests reaction speed and inner-ring patching</li>\n          <li><strong>Armor / Shield:</strong> Forces burst and sustained DPS</li>\n          <li><strong>Salvage dreadnought:</strong> Every 5 waves — failing here usually means early scrap conversion failed</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏁 Difficulty</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Easy:</strong> Learn three rings and salvage economy</li>\n          <li><strong>Normal:</strong> Upgrade priority and manual wave calls matter</li>\n          <li><strong>Hard:</strong> Faster spiral and higher HP — weak layering collapses into the core</li>\n        </ul>",
