      "helpBack": "Back to Menu",
      "helpHtml": "<h3>🎯 Battlefield Goal</h3>\n        <p>The <strong>core fission reactor</strong> at the center is the entire line's lifeline. Enemy machines flood in from the outer edges and rush the core on direct approach paths. Your job is not just to survive, but to convert limited ore into a stable kill zone that keeps every wave under control.</p>\n        <h3>⚔️ Match Rhythm</h3>\n        <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Deploy phase:</strong> Decide your opener, crossfire lanes, and core safety zone before you launch the raid</li>\n                  <li><strong>Combat phase:</strong> Consecutive kills raise your multiplier, and the multiplier accelerates your economy</li>\n                  <li><strong>Cleanup phase:</strong> Do not panic-build into leftovers; read which lane is actually collapsing</li>\n                  <li><strong>Wave control:</strong> Manual wave timing is often stronger than blindly enabling auto-next</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>👾 Enemy Read</h3>\n        <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Scout / Swarm:</strong> Fast pressure tools that test early fire density</li>\n                  <li><strong>Phantom / Shield:</strong> Demand focused fire and accurate tower placement</li>\n                  <li><strong>Heavy / Brood:</strong> Punish weak splash coverage and slow cleanup</li>\n                  <li><strong>Elite / Titan:</strong> True tempo checks; if these break you, your economy conversion failed earlier</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏭 Build Logic</h3>\n        <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Gun Tower:</strong> Reliable opener for stable early clearing</li>\n                  <li><strong>Laser / Frost:</strong> One burns priority targets, one controls lane speed</li>\n                  <li><strong>Sniper:</strong> Best used to finish high-threat units, not to pad general DPS</li>\n                  <li><strong>Mortar / Rocket:</strong> Strong around bends, clumps, and mixed late waves</li>\n                  <li><strong>Tesla:</strong> Becomes a mid-to-late anchor once enemy density rises</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🧠 Tactical Skills</h3>\n        <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Core Fission:</strong> A tempo reset tool — save it for real pressure spikes</li>\n                  <li><strong>Tower Overdrive:</strong> Best when several lanes peak at once and you need instant output</li>\n                  <li><strong>Airdrop Supply:</strong> Not just extra ore, but emergency funds for a key reposition or patch</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏁 Difficulty Read</h3>\n        <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Easy:</strong> Learn opener order, lane coverage, and manual wave flow</li>\n                  <li><strong>Normal:</strong> Resource planning and gap-patching start to matter every wave</li>\n                  <li><strong>Hard:</strong> Weak tower layering gets punished by faster multi-lane pressure</li>\n                  <li><strong>Extreme:</strong> Every ore spend must become real damage or control, or the whole line collapses</li>\n        </ul>",
