      "helpBack": "Back to Menu",
      "helpHtml": "<h3>🎯 Battlefield Goal</h3>\n        <p>Pilot a void fighter through a three-lane abyss corridor. Winning is not just dodging — it is using lane switches and dash to keep the combo multiplier alive so distance, waves, and grade climb together.</p>\n        <h3>⚔️ Match Rhythm</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Open:</strong> Find a stable switch rhythm before spam-dashing</li>\n          <li><strong>Mid:</strong> Orbs decide whether combo can roll high; missing orbs hurts long-term score more than one hit</li>\n          <li><strong>Wave gates:</strong> Every 5 waves is a rhythm checkpoint — read warnings before committing a lane</li>\n          <li><strong>Late:</strong> When hazards interweave, save shield and dash for truly undodgeable moments</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🕹️ Decision Inputs</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>A / D or arrows:</strong> Left / center / right lane</li>\n          <li><strong>Space dash:</strong> For walls you cannot dodge — not for random rushing</li>\n          <li><strong>Touch swipe:</strong> Same lane logic on mobile</li>\n          <li><strong>ESC / P:</strong> Pause, read the board, re-enter</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>⚡ Threat Read</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Energy barrier:</strong> Single-lane block — prefer switch; dash only if forced</li>\n          <li><strong>Pulse laser:</strong> Watch the warning flash before pre-moving</li>\n          <li><strong>Drifting mine:</strong> Cross-lane bait — late game you cannot tunnel-vision your lane</li>\n          <li><strong>BOSS waves:</strong> Waves 5 / 10 / 15+ are the real score watersheds</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>💎 Resources & Grade</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Energy orbs:</strong> Sustain combo (up to ×5); decays if ignored</li>\n          <li><strong>Shield core:</strong> One insurance hit — do not waste it in low-threat zones</li>\n          <li><strong>HP:</strong> 3 points — late HP is high-value score</li>\n          <li><strong>Grades:</strong> S ≥ 50000 · A ≥ 30000 · B ≥ 15000 · C ≥ 5000 · D below</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏁 Difficulty</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Casual:</strong> Learn switching, dash timing, and combo sustain</li>\n          <li><strong>Standard:</strong> Requires reading lasers and mine rhythm</li>\n          <li><strong>Abyss:</strong> Speed and density rise together — a broken combo is hard to recover</li>\n        </ul>",
