          "helpHtml": "<h3>🎯 Battlefield Goal</h3>\n        <p>This is not mindless DPS stacking. Climb from floor 1 to 15 and shape a deck that can block, kill, and arrive at bosses with the right tools ready.</p>\n        <h3>⚔️ Match Rhythm</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Early floors:</strong> Survive first — prioritize block and stable damage over flashy chains</li>\n          <li><strong>Mid:</strong> Elites and camps alternate — this is when the deck takes shape</li>\n          <li><strong>Boss gates:</strong> Every 5 floors is a real checkpoint; reading intent beats raw HP racing</li>\n          <li><strong>Endgame:</strong> Save burst and control before floor 15 — do not burn key cards on trash floors</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🃏 Play Decisions</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>3 energy</strong> per turn, hand cap 5; enemies act on intent after you end turn</li>\n          <li>Block clears at end of turn — a tempo tool, not permanent HP</li>\n          <li><strong>Void Relay:</strong> Play 3 same-type cards in a row for a pulse (bonus damage + draw)</li>\n          <li>Read statuses: Vulnerable, Burn, Mirror Shield rewrite trade math</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🌑 Abyss Systems</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li>After a floor win, pick 1 of 3 cards; too much junk collapses energy cycling</li>\n          <li>Elite every 4 floors; camps after every 3 floors or a boss (heal / refine / max HP)</li>\n          <li>Bosses under 50% HP <strong>enrage</strong> — dragging fights is usually a loss</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3>🏁 Difficulty</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Easy:</strong> Weaker enemies, wider player HP — learn intents and relay</li>\n          <li><strong>Normal:</strong> Balanced curve — deck building starts to matter</li>\n          <li><strong>Hard:</strong> Meaner enemies, thinner HP, higher score multiplier</li>\n        </ul>",
